<title>USA: Hollinger to buy back up to 3 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Hollinger to buy back up to 3 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hollinger International Inc said on Monday it intends to repurchase up to three million shares of its class A common shares and/or its preferred redeemable increased dividend equity securities (PRIDES) on the open market. No time frame has been established for the transactions, said the company,</p>
<p>Hollinger added that it believes both its class A common shares and its PRIDES are undervalued.</p>
<p>Hollinger is a newspaper publisher whose properties include The London Daily Telegraph, The Chicago Sun-Times and The Ottawa Citizen.</p>
